      "title": "Delete user route lacks admin check",
      "description": "The DELETE /admin/users/:id route does not use the requireAdmin middleware, but its sibling routes do. The server mounts the admin router without any router-wide auth in src/server.js:6. Any caller who can reach the server can delete any user by id. They can also enumerate ids to wipe the user table. Add requireAdmin to the route, as the GET and purge routes do.",
      "suggested_change": "admin.delete(\"/users/:id\", requireAdmin, async (req, res) => {",
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
