      "line_number": 22,
      "line_end": 24,
      "title": "Floating removeUser promises in purge loop",
      "description": "The purge handler passes an async callback to forEach, so nothing awaits or catches the removeUser promises. db.removeUser throws for an unknown id at src/db.js:10. One unknown id in the purge list causes an unhandled rejection, which crashes the Node process by default. The response also reports removals before any removal finishes. Await all removals with Promise.allSettled and count the fulfilled ones. Then respond with that count.",
      "suggested_change": "  const results = await Promise.allSettled(ids.map((id) => db.removeUser(id)));\n  res.json({ removed: results.filter((r) => r.status === \"fulfilled\").length });",
      "source": "lens:async-floating-promise",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The purge handler passes an async callback to forEach, so nothing awaits or catches the removeUser promises. db.removeUser throws for an unknown id at src/db.js:10.",
      "consequence": "One unknown id in the purge list causes an unhandled rejection, which crashes the Node process by default. The response also reports removals before any removal finishes.",
      "fix": "Await all removals with Promise.allSettled and count the fulfilled ones. Then respond with that count."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "file_path": "src/admin.js",
      "line_number": 25,
      "line_end": 25,
      "title": "Purge reports requested count as removed count",
      "description": "The purge handler returns ids.length as the removed count. It does this even when some removals fail or are still pending. Admins see a removed count that can be higher than the number of users actually deleted. Count only the successful removals after they settle.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": null,
